From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:20:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/20] [maglev] Bail out on functions whose merges could
 overflow a node's inputs

Equivalent of v8 24ae3662bf (M140 07ad1d3ae2; crbug 441668149) without its abort machinery: Maglev does not compile bytecode of kMaxInputs / 2 bytes or more, which bounds every merge's predecessor count. FlyWeb Maglev debt for level 134.

(cherry picked from commit a2fb7342fcfe7793f4a71aab87ca08093b2261bd)
(cherry picked from commit 37fbbeb2c3e8f8d89e6722ef308939480c75b8aa)
---
 src/maglev/maglev-compiler.cc | 18 +++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/maglev/maglev-compiler.cc b/src/maglev/maglev-compiler.cc
index 38e29607..3d6c5b13 100644
--- a/src/maglev/maglev-compiler.cc
+++ b/src/maglev/maglev-compiler.cc
@@ -97,14 +97,22 @@ bool MaglevCompiler::Compile(LocalIsolate* local_isolate,
       }
     }
 
-    // FlyWeb: port of v8 618d1a0290 (crbug 444048019). 13.3's graph builder
-    // cannot abort, so bail out before building when a SuspendGenerator could
-    // need more inputs than a node can hold (generators are never inlined).
+    // FlyWeb: 13.3's graph builder cannot abort (v8 24ae3662bf is not
+    // ported), so bail out before building when a node could need more inputs
+    // than it can hold:
+    // - a SuspendGenerator with too many registers (v8 618d1a0290, crbug
+    //   444048019; generators are never inlined);
+    // - a merge with too many predecessors (v8 24ae3662bf, crbug 441668149):
+    //   each predecessor (a jump, a fallthrough or a throwing bytecode) is a
+    //   bytecode of at least one byte and peeling counts one at most twice, so
+    //   a bytecode shorter than kMaxInputs / 2 cannot get there (TurboFan stops
+    //   at 60 KB anyway). Inlined functions are far below that.
     {
       MaglevCompilationUnit* unit = compilation_info->toplevel_compilation_unit();
       if (unit->parameter_count() + unit->register_count() +
-              GeneratorStore::kFixedInputCount >
-          Node::kMaxInputs) {
+                  GeneratorStore::kFixedInputCount >
+              Node::kMaxInputs ||
+          unit->bytecode().length() >= Node::kMaxInputs / 2) {
         return false;
       }
     }
